stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> OUTSIDE_GAME
    OUTSIDE_GAME --> PLAYING : start Classic
    OUTSIDE_GAME --> HANDOFF : start Pic-Pac Local
    OUTSIDE_GAME --> TURN_START : start Vs Computer or AI Lab

    HANDOFF --> REVEALING : Ready / draw once and remove held piece
    TURN_START --> REVEALING : current presentation finishes / draw once
    REVEALING --> PLAYING : reveal finishes / human or local actor
    REVEALING --> AI_TARGETING : reveal finishes / computer decision already ready
    REVEALING --> AI_THINKING : reveal finishes / computer decision pending
    AI_THINKING --> AI_TARGETING : valid computer decision arrives
    AI_TARGETING --> AI_PLACING : current presentation finishes / commit selected move
    AI_PLACING --> AI_SETTLING : current presentation finishes
    AI_SETTLING --> TURN_START : current presentation finishes / nonterminal
    AI_SETTLING --> TERMINAL : current presentation finishes / terminal

    PLAYING --> PLAYING : legal nonterminal Classic placement
    PLAYING --> HANDOFF : legal nonterminal Local placement
    PLAYING --> TURN_START : legal nonterminal human placement vs Computer
    PLAYING --> TERMINAL : human or Classic placement ends game

    TERMINAL --> PLAYING : Classic rematch / alternate starter
    TERMINAL --> HANDOFF : Local rematch / alternate starter
    TERMINAL --> TURN_START : Computer rematch / alternate starter

    HANDOFF --> OUTSIDE_GAME : Home or Back / abandon game
    TURN_START --> OUTSIDE_GAME : Home or Back / cancel work
    REVEALING --> OUTSIDE_GAME : Back / cancel work
    PLAYING --> OUTSIDE_GAME : Home or Back / abandon game
    AI_THINKING --> OUTSIDE_GAME : Home or Back / cancel work
    AI_TARGETING --> OUTSIDE_GAME : Home or Back / cancel work
    AI_PLACING --> OUTSIDE_GAME : Home or Back / abandon committed game
    AI_SETTLING --> OUTSIDE_GAME : Home or Back / abandon committed game
    TERMINAL --> OUTSIDE_GAME : Home or Back

    note right of REVEALING
        Human and computer symbols use the same visible reveal.
        Computer search starts here, off the main thread.
        Fast search must not shorten the reveal.
    end note
    note right of AI_THINKING
        No fixed presentation timer.
        Board remains locked until the decision is ready.
    end note
    note right of AI_PLACING
        Board is already committed, including a terminal move.
        Display Computer through AI_SETTLING even if
        domain activePlayer has changed to the human.
    end note
    note left of TURN_START
        Timed callbacks require GAME screen and matching presentationId.
        Domain commit also requires matching revision and turn token.
        Reduced Motion changes delays and decoration, not state order.
    end note
